Cluster Maintenance: Cluster Components like kube-apiserver; controller-manager; etcd cluster and so on can have different versions. Since kube-apiserver is the main guy in the cluster where all components talk to, No component version must be higher than the kube-apiserver except for kubectl component. Kubernetes supports only upto three recent minor updates.
 three strategies:
Strategy1: has downtime. Master upgrades and then after that all nodes at a time. When Master is being upgraded/down kubectl no longer works. Can't add/delete/edit pods/nodes. And all nodes would be accessible unless their pod fails for some reason.
Strategy 2: No downtime. nodes upgrading one at a time.
Strategy 3: No downtime. Add extra nodes with already upgrades version then shift the pods to that.
